From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:27:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: chapter person
 files and map settings laid in the read

Engine round E1 (F-046 / F-047, round 59). Two new file kinds in the patch file,
both patched only inside the game's own read of its RomFS, like the placements:

- `person`: `GameData/Person/**` (the chapter person files and the route-variant
  HANDOVER files; `Person::Load` 0x0044A808 builds `GameData/Person/%s.bin.lz` when
  the game needs one). This lays the character shuffle's route-variant rows ("keep the
  face"), enemy levels and tougher bosses from the in-game page.
- `mapconfig`: `map/config/<chapter>.bin`, stored plain (the format string
  `map/config/%s.bin` in the game's code): the chapter's map theme names (music).

`v` cells may now also lie in the file's string pool (offset at or past the pool
start, never inside the relocation or label lists, same length): the music track
writes a new song name over the old one in place, never longer (Grok's pick A,
docs/collab/E1_MUSIC_GROK.md), so these files keep their exact size and need no label
pointers. A label pointer in a person or map settings file is refused and the file is
served unchanged with a notice (there is no in-memory path for them); a plain file
must keep its exact size. Files of these kinds that cannot be laid say so ("chapter
people kept original", "map settings kept original").

Without an active randomized run nothing changes: the hooks return at once as before.
Checked: `cargo test -p zakuro-core --lib` 180 passed (new test
plain_file_pool_cells_and_refusals); made_patch_fits_the_real_files with a made patch
(seed e1a: shuffle route, music maps+battles, enemy levels 2, bosses linear) on the
clean dump: all 110 person files and 99 map settings files fit and show every new cell.
